    {
      "id": "de766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e6766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Communication Sciences and Disorders program is organized for students to begin in the Fall semester. If students begin in the Spring, it will take an extra semester to finish the undergraduate curriculum. Students must have a 2.5 GPA in the major in order to graduate with a B.S. in Communication Sciences and Disorders. Students are strongly advised to complete all undergraduate General Education units before beginning major coursework. It is strongly recommended students complete a course in Physics and/or Chemistry as some programs offering the Master's Degree in Speech Language Pathology or Communication Sciences and Disorders will require it. In lieu of CHDV 30, CSAD will approve any other course in Human Development or Developmental Psychology across the Lifespan (birth through death must be covered). In lieu of DEAF 51, CSAD will approve any course in Sign Language. In lieu of PSYC 2, CSAD will approve any Introductory Psychology course. In lieu of STAT 1, CSAD will accept a course in Introductory Statistics. For additional information, please visit: Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Communication Sciences and Disorders program is organized for students to begin in the Fall semester. If students begin in the Spring, it will take an extra semester to finish the undergraduate curriculum.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must have a 2.5 GPA in the major in order to graduate with a B.S. in Communication Sciences and Disorders. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students are strongly advised to complete all undergraduate General Education units before beginning major coursework.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is strongly recommended students complete a course in Physics and/or Chemistry as some programs offering the Master's Degree in Speech Language Pathology or Communication Sciences and Disorders will require it. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In lieu of CHDV 30, CSAD will approve any other course in Human Development or Developmental Psychology across the Lifespan (birth through death must be covered). </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In lieu of DEAF 51, CSAD will approve any course in Sign Language. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In lieu of PSYC 2, CSAD will approve any Introductory Psychology course.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In lieu of STAT 1, CSAD will accept a course in Introductory Statistics.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/health-human-services/communication-sciences-disorders/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
